	>*/


	/* NOTE (TableFilterAge, EN )
	>
	>PARAMETER
	>Tabulation restriction: Age (current)
	>
	>LOCATION	Base(Tabulation_Control).dat
	>LAST UPDATE	June 2019
	>
	>DESCRIPTION	Range of ages for which tabulation should be performed.
	>
	>DIMENSIONS
	>[cLOWER_UPPER_BOUNDS]
	>
	>
	>SOURCE
	>
	>DEFINITION
	>
	>METHODS	Tabulation in POHEM are restricted to a population of interest define
	by the following set of 9 parameters.
	>*Sex(es) must be within those selected in parameter "Tabulation restriction:
	Sex".
	>*Province(s) must be within those selected in parameter "Tabulation
	restriction: Province".
	>*Education level(s) must be within those selected in parameter "Tabulation
	restriction: Education".
	>*Income level(s) must be within those selected in parameter "Tabulation
	restriction: Income quartile".
	>*Point(s) of entry must be within those selected in parameter "Tabulation
	restriction: Entry point/door".
	>*Age must be within the bounds provided by parameter "Tabulation restriction:
	Age (current)".
	>*Initial age must be within the bounds provided by parameter "Tabulation
	restriction: Initial age (upon actor creation)".
	>*Year must be within the bounds provided by parameter "Tabulation
	restriction: Year (current)".
	>*Initial year must be within the bounds provided by parameter "Tabulation
	restriction: Initial year (upon actor creation)".
	>
	>Note that some tables may have additional conditions that further restrict the
	population tabulated.
	>
	>ASSUMPTIONS
	>
	>DECISIONS
	>
	>REFERENCES
	>
	>COMMENTS	The default scenario calls for no specific restriction.  Therefore
	only "additional conditions" specific to each table will restrict the
	population tabulated.
	>
