	>Initial dementia alteration: In scope years
	>
	>LOCATION
	>LAST UPDATE	June 2021
	>
	>DESCRIPTION	Years over which the alignment of POHEM’s initial dementia status
	with some target is done.
	>
	>DIMENSIONS
	>[cLOWER_UPPER_BOUNDS]
	>
	>
	>SOURCE
	>
	>DEFINITION
	>
	>METHODS	Parameters “Initial dementia alteration: In scope populations” and
	“Initial dementia alteration: In scope years” tell POHEM who is subject to
	alteration of their dementia status read in from the StartPop file (parameter
	“Distribution of population at beginning of simulation”).
	>
	>ASSUMPTIONS
	>
	>DECISIONS
	>
	>REFERENCES
	>
	>COMMENTS
	>
	>
	>
	>*//* NOTE (WeightForUnderlyingDemportUniform, EN )
	>
	>PARAMETER
	>Initial dementia alteration: Correspondence with dementia risk
	>
	>LOCATION
	>LAST UPDATE	June 2021
	>
	>DESCRIPTION	The parameter allows users to select the methods used to ensure
	that POHEM’s initial dementia distribution agrees with some target.
	>
	>DIMENSIONS
	>None
	>
	>SOURCE
	>
	>DEFINITION
	>
	>METHODS	The parameter “Initial dementia alteration: Correspondence with
	dementia risk” (called w hereafter) is used to tell which method to use to
	insure that initial dementia prevalence lines up with some target.
	>* 	If |w| > 1 then the initial dementia alteration is turned off.
	>* 	If |w| <= 1 then a method is used to ensure that the distribution of initial
	dementia status of people entering the simulation in 2001 agrees with that of
	parameter “Initial dementia alteration: prevalence by age, sex and province for
	year 2001”. The method used ensures that targets are met with minimal
	alteration to people’s dementia status.  The scope of this adjustment is
	restricted by parameters “Initial dementia alteration: In scope populations”
	and “Initial dementia alteration: In scope years”
	>
	>The results will depend on w and has an impact on who will see their initial
	dementia status altered.  Here are some key values
	>* 	w=1: If, in a given province, sex, and age group category, more people with
	dementia are required, then those who did not initially have dementia but are
	at high risk of dementia (according to a risk equation similar to DemPoRT) will
	see their initial dementia status changed from NO to YES. By contrast, if fewer
	people with dementia are required, then those who initially had dementia but
	are at low risk of dementia (according to a risk equation similar to DemPoRT)
	will see their initial dementia status changed from YES to NO.
	>* 	w=-1: This does things backwards relative to w=1. In short, POHEM will
	change an actor’s initial dementia status from NO to YES if (DemPoRT-like) risk
	of dementia is low, and from YES to NO if risk of dementia is high. This is a
	somewhat silly option.
	>* 	w=0: The (DemPoRT-like) risk of dementia is not used to decide who will get
	an altered initial dementia status.  It is random.
	>
	>
	>ASSUMPTIONS
	>DECISIONS	Value set to w=1 in base scenario.
	>
	>REFERENCES
	>
	>COMMENTS
	>

	>
	>*/

};
